# Line endings are LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true at system scope, so without this file
# a Windows clone checks every text file out as CRLF. Anything that then writes
# LF - an editor, a script, an agent with filesystem access - produces a
# whitespace-only diff across the whole file, and real changes get lost in it.
# Declaring the intent here makes it a property of the repository rather than
# of whoever happens to have cloned it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
